  "body": "Add the opt-in NXMMU x86 EFI consumer for the native stage-1 Rust memory provider. Authored code fetches and transfers through nonidentity 4K/16K lower/upper mappings, including discontiguous pair accesses and precise translation/access/permission/backing/attribute failures. Both ISE dependencies pin720d7c6; Core remains40833dc. Existing firmware features and source ownership remain intact.\n\nThe host reader independently checks all108 identities and numeric results, input/runner hashes, and rejects missing, duplicated or malformed fields. The actual Win64 C/Rust ABI and full RAM/register checks run inside EFI. A separately compiled wrong-VA-as-PA control fails on first fetch without invented guest syndrome. Generated Python bytecode is excluded from source/inventory.\n\nValidation: fresh standalone final commit with empty Cargo cache builds default/direct/combined and NXMMU from canonical Git dependencies, passes all-feature UEFI checks,13 strict conditional provider cases,108 actual stage-1 OVMF cases and4 reader tests, and leaves a clean checkout. Historical binary and source-patch validation remain separately recorded.\n\nThis verifies the fixed immutable Normal-NC/A=1 profile; dynamic MMU changes, normal macOS startup and guest Metal are subsequent work.",
